# Tamil Nadu Crime Prediction System

### Machine Learning-Based Crime Analysis and Prediction Dashboard

A web-based crime analysis and prediction system developed using **Python, Machine Learning, and Streamlit**. The application provides crime data visualization, city-wise analysis, machine learning predictions, an interactive crime map, a local data intelligence assistant, and downloadable PDF reports.

The project demonstrates how data science and machine learning can be integrated into an interactive web application for crime data analysis.

## Live Application

**[View the Deployed Website](https://sreedharshini115-tamilnadu-crime-prediction-app-hgtook.streamlit.app/)**

**Deployment Platform:** Streamlit Community Cloud

## Project Overview

The Tamil Nadu Crime Prediction System is designed to analyze historical sample crime data and estimate crime counts based on selected input parameters.

The application uses a **Random Forest Regressor** to generate predictions and presents results through an interactive, emergency command center-style dashboard.

The system is developed as an educational machine learning project and does not use live police crime records.

## Key Features

### 1. Crime Analytics Dashboard
- Displays crime data summaries and key metrics.
- Provides city-wise crime count comparisons.
- Visualizes crime category distributions.
- Shows year-wise crime trends.
- Includes an interactive dataset preview.

### 2. Machine Learning Crime Prediction
- Uses the Random Forest Regression algorithm.
- Predicts estimated crime counts.
- Accepts city, year, crime category, and population as inputs.
- Calculates estimated crime rates per 100,000 people.
- Displays prediction results through dashboard metrics.

### 3. Interactive Crime Map
- Displays Tamil Nadu city locations.
- Uses geographical coordinates from the dataset.
- Visualizes aggregated sample crime counts.
- Supports interactive geographical exploration.

### 4. Data Intelligence Assistant
- Provides a local rule-based analytics assistant.
- Answers supported questions about the dataset.
- Identifies cities with high sample crime counts.
- Displays crime category comparisons and yearly trends.
- Retrieves the latest generated prediction.

### 5. PDF Report Generation
- Generates downloadable prediction reports.
- Includes city, year, crime category, and population.
- Displays predicted crime counts and estimated crime rates.
- Provides a structured report suitable for project demonstrations.

### 6. Emergency Command Center Interface
- Professional dark-themed dashboard.
- Structured navigation and analytics sections.
- Responsive interface.
- Dedicated prediction, map, assistant, and reporting workspaces.

